# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #exceptions: an implicit throw is caught by its name across calls; call joins the implicit
# names by the general mechanism): the failed admission inside inner, which declares Oops, leaves inner as its implicit
# call and reaches run, which takes it by catch: call although its catch: Oops pad stands first. A declared name
# keyed like call, or a status not remapped across inner, lands in the Oops handler (84) or stops the Message. Entry 7.
S:
    int: x 9
    int: y 2
end: S
D:
    int: x 1
end: D
fn: inner () int
    throws: Oops
    call: S D
    if: D\x = 0
        throw: Oops
    return: 1
end: inner
fn: run () int
    int: r 82
    r: inner()
    catch: Oops ()
        r: 84
    ---
    catch: call ()
        r: 83
        if: D\x = 1
            r: 7
    ---
return: r
int: got run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
